              "pages": {
                "end": 26,
                "start": 26
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Ms. Harrington, congress has statutes indicating that intervenors may not need standing without a subsequent assessment."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Dvoretsky",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0002-0005"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 50,
                "start": 50
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Dvoretsky, an intervenor of right is not unlimited; there are limits on what that intervenor can do."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0002"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 59,
                "start": 59
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Katyal, a mandatory intervenor under Rule\u202f24(a)(2) is a full party and can issue subpoenas or document requests without court oversight."
        },
        {
          "attribution": "Mr. Katyal",
          "citations": [
            {
              "document_hash": "5f5a0eb0504cc6c066057b59a1d2471d34978fc57ecfcd47c9f86b7594105769",
              "evidence_ids": [
                "ev-5f5a0eb0504c-0003-0003"
              ],
              "pages": {
                "end": 60,
                "start": 60
              }
            }
          ],
          "text": "According to Mr. Katyal, intervenors have much more power under Rule\u202f24(b) than under Rule\u202f24(a)(2)."
        }
